quirement\":\"Provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol: pre-restart baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, and recovered service/data/MAC state\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Pre-restart boot_id f43afa1c... and healthy state captured; backgrounded systemctl reboot returned an ack before disconnect; a subsequent poll timed out (proving the node actually went down) then succeeded with a new boot_id 18c8b181...; post-restart state shows SELinux Enforcing, httpd active/enabled under httpd_t, port 8181 listening, firewall rule and semanage port mapping intact, and the Widget/42 row persisted. The fixed lifecycle snapshots corroborate the boot_id change and show no failed services after executor.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-2203aa4e1a46439c\",\"cmd-124282d6317442ac\",\"cmd-bf1b16b747bf4541\",\"cmd-5254ccd2b5b6455e\",\"cmd-1a1e7abf70964046\",\"cmd-fd3668aac63e4688\"]}],\"confidence\":0.88,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.85,\"summary\":\"State-changing commands (package install, CGI app creation, httpd vhost config, semanage port/fcontext labeling, chown/chmod fix for a genuine DAC bug, firewalld port open, reboot) all map directly to satisfying the task or the mandatory restart protocol; no destructive or unrelated mutations were found. Minor residue: /tmp/inventory.py, /tmp/resp.html, and /tmp/reboot.log were left behind after use (visible in the after-executor temp-files snapshot) rather than cleaned up — low-severity, non-security-impacting leftover scratch files. The semanage port listing shows both http_port_t and intermapper_port_t associated with '8181' after the -a call, which is unexplained (though functional testing and httpd_t confinement confirm the bind actually succeeds under policy).\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-21d939ed63e84f6b\",\"global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files\",\"global:after_executor:node1:failed-services\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"All material outcomes of the task — inventory app functioning over TCP 8181 on node1, SELi